  "service_latency_findings": [
    "api.js journals job.start before dispatch and journals completion before replying. Each Journal.save performs file sync, rename and directory sync; a successful journaled operation therefore has two service publications in addition to worker persistence. No barrier was removed.",
    "The preceding S90D native root outlier spent 1138.673 ms inside its HTTPS request versus 1141.376 ms in the outer harness measurement; local journal writes explain only about 2.703 ms of that sample, not its one-second delay.",
    "The preceding managed app forget outlier spent 1547.874 ms in its HTTPS RPC. Existing timing cannot partition TLS/network, coordinator journal begin, worker execution and journal finish.",
    "The earlier S90D preflight had 638 request rows and its integrated harness traced 101 journaled requests. Those observations do not point to the 1000-row archive threshold as the cause; phase timing is still needed rather than inferring a storage mechanism.",
    "Native saved job timestamps have whole-second precision, which is too coarse to resolve the required subintervals. The next implementation step is authenticated server-side phase timing around journal begin, worker execution and journal finish, preserving request semantics and persistence barriers."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "One counterbalanced pair of 20-second idle runs per TV is a bounded comparison, not a statistical overhead distribution. CPU deltas cover the first-to-last sample interval and exclude observer launch/persistence.",
    "PSS plus Swap is a sampled accounting proxy, not exact physical memory ownership. Baseline has twenty mapping observations; the reduced observer has four. Resident pages and lifetime peak RSS remain sampled every tick.",
    "Mapping details are now sampled every fifth tick and on each new PID/start/executable identity. Null fast-row fields are intentionally unsampled; do not carry forward stale detail values. Short mapping peaks may be missed.",
    "The full 8 MiB resource capacity remains reserved, but only populated pages are dirtied. Page faults during buffer growth are included in observer cost. Kernel collection retains its 2 MiB prefaulted buffer.",
    "The first intermediate paired comparison, before discovery filtering, reduced CPU by roughly 30 percent and is retained privately. Reported final binaries also skip unrelated proc stat/cmdline reads.",
    "The fresh integrated rounds did not reproduce one-second admissions; that does not resolve previous outliers or close the no-regression gate. The observer still has nonzero CPU, memory and scheduling effects.",
    "Installed worker/service bytes and .NET bridge/fallback/recovery are unchanged. No reboot, standby, global policy, persistent capability or SMACK change was issued. Endurance, native-only entry and native-default observation remain open."
  ]
}
